  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Out-Of-Site Camp Management Recovery Support for Internally Displaced Persons and Host Communities Affected by Cyclones Bastirai and Emnati</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The East coast of Madagascar was hit in February 2022 by two cyclones (Bastirai and Emnati) causing the displacement of thousands of people who found refuge in displacement sites. In two regions (Vatovavy and Fitovinany) nearly 141,800 people saw their homes destroyed. An IOM/WFP rapid assessment undertaken in April 2022 indicates that 30% of households with destroyed houses are still living with host families, and 25% of households said that one or more family members moved. This project is contributing to the efforts of the Government of Madagascar and its humanitarian partners in data collection on internally displaced persons (IDPs), providing support on income generating activities and contribute to building capacities of IDPs and host communities and partners in Eastern Madagascar, particularly men, women, girl and boys, including persons with disabilities, as well as the hosting communities.</narrative>
  </description>
